A||||1||PaUL||Exhaust leak fix
Z||000000||PaUL||06-21-99||04:13 PM||||Hi, this weekend I came up with an amazing way of fixing leaky exhaust manifolds on the 2.8. Its so amazing, I even amazed myself when I thought it up. For years now Ive been living with leaking exhaust manifolds. They leak because they dont fit flush against the heads. I gave up on trying to fix this a long time ago. Everytime I'd change the gasket, it would start leaking in a matter of days. After awhile I stopped using any gaskets at all. Last Saturday I was in a hardware store and saw something unusual, seamless brass rings the exact size of the exhaust ports. I bought 6 of them and rushed home. I unbolted just the rear manifold and super glued the rings onto the ports, then bolted it back on. The glue just holds the rings in place when installing the manifold. When I started it up, there was no exhaust leak noise! I couldnt believe it, after all these years I finally figured out a way to seal the leaks up.
Z||000001||GREENDANO||06-21-99||07:04 PM||||Nice find,  I paid $45 for a set of copper header gaskets for my big block Ford last year.  Sounds like you got out a lot cheaper but just as effectively.<br>   Dan-O
